    "about-founder": {
      "type": "page-about-split",
      "settings": {
        "image_url": "https://barreletics.com/cdn/shop/files/43879272_2264664830242380_3230081226412916736_n.jpg?v=1613762916&width=1600",
        "image_alt": "Stefanie Miller, founder of Barreletics",
        "media_column_pct": 50,
        "title": "Fashion trained the eye. The studio set the standard.",
        "body": "<p>A former career as a fashion model took me around the world: design, textiles, architecture, craftsmanship, the details that elevate an experience.</p><p>That foundation meets a practice I take seriously. At the time, grippy yoga socks were the only tool available. They slipped when grip mattered most, required constant adjusting, and never delivered the control they promised.</p><p>I found myself breaking focus to fix my socks instead of holding the position, sliding out of side planks, resetting my feet. Fabric holds moisture. I wanted a clean, connected practice.</p><p>If I was dedicating an hour to my practice, I wanted that hour to count: secure, grounded, connected, and confident. And I knew I was not the only one.</p>",
        "reverse": false,
        "mobile_stack_order": "media_first",
        "aria_label": "Stefanie Miller — founder",
        "media_max_px": 760,
        "media_max_px_mobile": 480,
        "cream_bg": false,
